Subject: [PATCH] client: run against Engine OS's QtGui, and take a mouse as touch
Applies-to: qtwayland-everywhere-src-6.7.2 (download.qt.io release tarball)
Modified-files: src/client/*.cpp, src/client/*_p.h, src/plugins/shellintegration/
                xdg-shell/qwaylandxdgshell.cpp (LGPL-3.0-only OR GPL-2.0-only OR
                GPL-3.0-only, per their headers); src/client/CMakeLists.txt
                (BSD-3-Clause); new src/client/qtgui_wayland_iface.cpp, taken from
                qtbase's src/gui/platform/unix/qunixnativeinterface.cpp (same
                license as the client sources)
Modified-by: Peyton Cashin <66343323+Peyton-C@users.noreply.github.com>, 2026-11-03
License: offered under the license of each file it modifies. This patch is NOT
         covered by the MIT LICENSE at the root of this repository. See
         ./README.md.

Engine OS ships QtGui 6.7.2 built without the cursor, sessionmanager and
wayland features, and without QtWaylandClient. build_qtwayland.sh builds a
qtbase configured the same way and this client against it, for the client to
load into Engine's own QtGui. Three changes make that possible, three make
Engine usable in it:

  * qtgui_wayland_iface.cpp: the QNativeInterface::QWaylandApplication,
    QWaylandScreen and Private::QWaylandWindow interfaces, which QtGui defines
    only with its wayland feature on, so Engine's has none of them. Defined in
    the client instead. build_qtwayland.sh generates the moc file it includes.

  * cursor guards: the client mostly builds without QtGui's cursor feature
    already; createPlatformCursor(), QWaylandDisplay::reconnect() and the
    xdg-shell popup enter events did not.

  * QT_WAYLAND_MOUSE_AS_TOUCH=1: QWaylandWindow delivers the left mouse button
    as a single touch point. Engine ignores mouse clicks, and under eglfs
    touchbridge does the same conversion; under a compositor the compositor
    owns the mouse.

  * QT_WAYLAND_SCREEN_SIZE=WxH: QWaylandScreen reports that size. Engine lays
    itself out for the screen and not its window, so in a window smaller than
    the output it was cropped; under eglfs the two are always the same.

  * keyboard: QtGui's xkbcommon feature is off as well, and without it the
    client drops every key. CMakeLists.txt builds QtGui's own xkbcommon helper
    (qxkbcommon*.cpp, copied from qtbase by build_qtwayland.sh) into the client
    and links libxkbcommon, which Engine OS ships.
